<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Texcoco</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texcoco">Texcoco</a> was a large lake in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a>, now largely drained. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztecs</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> on an island in the lake, connecting it to the shore by causeways. Its waters supported chinampa agriculture and canoe transport, which underpinned the economy of the Aztec Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-texcoco.jpg" alt="Lake Texcoco" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yavidaxiu; historicair 13:51, 11 September 2007 (UTC); derivative work by Sémhur · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Basin_of_Mexico_1519_map-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
